WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.070
Two roads race a byte across a desk.

2
00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:07.190
On the one-lane road, the bits
queue up and go one at a time.

3
00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.550
On the other, all 8 go side by side.

4
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.770
Over this short distance, the
eight-lane road wins easily.

5
00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.710
Next, the race moves across a whole room.

6
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.815
But first, look at the
plug on almost everything:

7
00:00:20.865 --> 00:00:25.070
USB, the Universal Serial Bus.

8
00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:30.570
If parallel moves more data at once,
why would USB pick the one-lane road?

9
00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:35.610
In this mission, you'll see how serial
and parallel transmission send their bits.

10
00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.550
You'll also find out
which ways data can flow:

11
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.070
simplex, half-duplex and full-duplex.

12
00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:46.400
Your mission: explain why
USB uses serial transmission.
